# Keep the Docker build context small. The API/Engine images use a NARROW context
# (publish/<app>); only the Web image uses the repo root, and Dockerfile.web copies just web/.
# Before this file existed the whole repo (mobile/, output/, Docs, bin/obj, node_modules…) was
# sent to the daemon on every web build.

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Build outputs
**/bin
**/obj
**/out
# Runner-published .NET output (the API/Engine images take publish/<app> as their own context).
**/publish

# Node / frontend deps (the web image runs its own pnpm install)
**/node_modules

# Heavy trees not needed by ANY image build
mobile
Docs
output
uploads
samples

# Test results & projects
**/TestResults
**/*.Tests

# Dockerfiles / compose are passed via -f; not needed inside the context
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile*

# Docs / editor / local dev / secrets
*.md
!README.md
**/*.user
**/.env*
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json
